In coding, a toolkit is a collection of pre-written code, software programs, and documents used to build applications faster

In JavaScript, a CDN (Content Delivery Network) is a globally distributed system of servers used to host and deliver JavaScript files, libraries, and frameworks

Instead of downloading a library (like jQuery or Bootstrap) and hosting it on your own server, you link directly to a copy hosted on a CDN.

