Boilerplate code refers to sections of code that must be included in multiple places with little or no modification to get a program running


Tailwind CSS is a utility-first CSS framework used to rapidly style websites directly inside your HTML or JavaScript components. 

Unlike traditional frameworks like Bootstrap that give you pre-built components (like a standard .btn class for buttons), Tailwind provides low-level, single-purpose building blocks. These classes map directly to standard CSS properties, allowing you to create completely custom designs without writing a single line of custom CSS.